1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,751
Step three.

2
00:00:01,751 --> 00:00:03,432
Create your environment inside Claude Code.

3
00:00:03,432 --> 00:00:06,235
Note that after installing and opening your Claude desktop app,

4
00:00:06,235 --> 00:00:09,878
note that you have to select the Code section of the Claude desktop

5
00:00:09,878 --> 00:00:11,279
app.

6
00:00:11,279 --> 00:00:14,642
Now, on the Claude Code interface, you need to create your environment.

7
00:00:14,642 --> 00:00:17,164
Such environment is where you will run command prompts,

8
00:00:17,164 --> 00:00:19,405
instructions, and edits for creating your motion graphics.

9
00:00:19,405 --> 00:00:21,087
So, how do we create one?

10
00:00:21,087 --> 00:00:22,488
Just watch.

11
00:00:22,488 --> 00:00:25,851
On the Claude interface, you click Choose Environment in the drop-down menu.

12
00:00:25,851 --> 00:00:27,252
Choose New Environment.

13
00:00:27,252 --> 00:00:30,895
A new environment box shows up under Local and the name My App

14
00:00:30,895 --> 00:00:32,296
Space.

15
00:00:32,296 --> 00:00:34,538
You can name it the project folder name.

16
00:00:34,538 --> 00:00:38,181
Under Folder, click Plus Add and select the project folder you created on

17
00:00:38,181 --> 00:00:39,582
your computer desktop.

18
00:00:39,582 --> 00:00:42,664
After that, click Create Environment to finally create your own environment.

19
00:00:42,664 --> 00:00:45,466
Once done, it will reflect on your Claude desktop area,

20
00:00:45,466 --> 00:00:46,868
as you can see here.

21
00:00:46,868 --> 00:00:48,549
If not selected, please select it.

22
00:00:48,549 --> 00:00:49,950
Let's move to step four.
